---
const faq = [
  {
    q: 'Is it free?',
    a: 'Yes. Pomodoro is free and open source under the MIT license. The code, the sounds and the icon are all in the GitHub repository.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why is there no installer?',
    a: 'On Windows there is nothing to install: unzip the archive anywhere, run Pomodoro.exe, optionally tick “Start with Windows” in settings. To uninstall, delete the folder and, if you like, %AppData%\\PomodoroTimer. On the Mac the download is a disk image: open it and drag Pomodoro to Applications.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Windows SmartScreen or macOS Gatekeeper complains on first launch. Is that normal?',
    a: 'Yes, for now. The builds are not signed with a paid certificate. On Windows click “More info”, then “Run anyway”. On the Mac click Done, then System Settings → Privacy & Security → Open Anyway, once (right-click → Open no longer works on macOS 15 and newer). You can also build the app yourself from the source: the .NET 8 SDK on Windows, the Command Line Tools on a Mac.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which download should I pick?',
    a: 'Windows: the self-contained zip is the safe choice, it runs on any 64-bit Windows 10 or 11; the framework-dependent zip is a fraction of the size but needs the .NET 8 Desktop Runtime. Mac: the .dmg, or the zip if you prefer to place the app yourself. Both Mac builds are universal and need macOS 13 or newer.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does it collect anything or need an account?',
    a: 'No. It never goes online. The only files it writes are settings.json, a small activity.log with timer events and error.log, in %AppData%\\PomodoroTimer on Windows and ~/Library/Application Support/PomodoroTimer on the Mac.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I use my own sounds?',
    a: 'Yes. In Settings → Sound, click the folder icon and pick any WAV or MP3. The eight built-in sounds were synthesized by a script, so they are free to use too.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I reset the timer if I switched tabs?',
    a: 'You don’t need to. Tabs only show a phase; the countdown keeps running on its own tab, marked with a dot. Click the “Focus running” line or the tab to get back. Only the “Start break” button actually switches phases.',
  },
];
---

<section id="faq" class="border-t border-line dark:border-line-dark">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-12 px-6 py-24 md:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr]">
    <div>
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide text-focus uppercase">FAQ</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-4xl">Questions people ask</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink-muted dark:text-ink-muted-dark">
        Something else? <a href="https://github.com/Shimodos/PomodoroTimer/issues" class="font-medium text-ink underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-ink dark:text-ink-dark dark:decoration-line-dark dark:hover:decoration-ink-dark">Open an issue</a> on GitHub.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="divide-y divide-line rounded-2xl border border-line bg-card dark:divide-line-dark dark:border-line-dark dark:bg-card-dark">
      {faq.map((item) => (
        <details class="group px-6 py-5 open:bg-paper/60 dark:open:bg-paper-dark/40">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-medium tracking-tight [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            {item.q}
            <span class="grid size-7 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-paper text-ink-muted transition group-open:rotate-45 dark:bg-paper-dark dark:text-ink-muted-dark" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 pr-10 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted dark:text-ink-muted-dark">{item.a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
